AArch64 handshake
"A post against the retirement of its generation and the drain of its consumer, contract 0.19 section 9.5, decision D-54"
(*
 * P0 is scada_queue_post on an event queue (libs/scada-tag/src/
 * queue_access.cpp, post_record): the first load of the state
 * (HeaderView::retiring, LDAR), the store of the record (here only the
 * store that publishes it matters), the store of write_seq
 * (publish_write_seq, STLR), and the second load of the state (LDAR). Both
 * loads find RUNNING (0 here) when the post returns SCADA_OK.
 *
 * P1 is scada-tagd setting the state to RETIRING (3;
 * HeaderView::set_retiring, STLR).
 *
 * P2 is the drain of the consumer (Queue::next in a RETIRING generation):
 * the load of the state (HeaderView::retiring, LDAR), which finds
 * RETIRING, then the load of write_seq (queue_write_seq_sc, LDAR).
 *
 * The condition is the loss the handshake forbids: the post returned
 * SCADA_OK (both its loads gave 0) and the drain that saw RETIRING missed
 * its record (write_seq 0). seq_cst loads and stores compile to LDAR and
 * STLR on Armv8.0, as acquire and release do; model_check.py also runs
 * copies with each access made plain.
 *)
{
0:X0=ws; 0:X1=st;
1:X1=st;
2:X0=ws; 2:X1=st;
}
 P0             | P1            | P2            ;
 LDAR W4,[X1]   | MOV W5,#3     | LDAR W6,[X1]  ;
 MOV W7,#1      | STLR W5,[X1]  | LDAR W8,[X0]  ;
 STLR W7,[X0]   |               |               ;
 LDAR W9,[X1]   |               |               ;
exists (0:X4=0 /\ 0:X9=0 /\ 2:X6=3 /\ 2:X8=0)
